<title>NORWAY: Aker settles dispute, to pay NOK 340 mln.</title>
<headline>Aker settles dispute, to pay NOK 340 mln.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian construction and offshore group Aker ASA said on Thursday it had settled a dispute with the Insurance Group of the Sleipner A platform.</p>
<p>Under the settlement all claims made by the Insurance Group in connection with the loss of the Sleipner platform have been withdrawn in exchange for the payment of 340 million crowns as of January 31, 1997.</p>
<p>Aker said the payment did not represent an admission of any liability for the loss.</p>
</text>
